  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhance National and Local Capacities to Combat TIP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To build and strengthen the government along with local organizations to respond to victims of trafficking. The project will build government and local capacity to respond to TIP victims in BiH through improved protection, prevention, and prosecution, and will be implemented across 30 BiH local municipalities. WV plans to improve provision of protection services that lead to victims and survivors achieving sustainable livelihoods and community and family resilience; help advance implementation of the multi-disciplinary national referral mechanism (NRM); and raise awareness on human trafficking and risk factors for first responders, medical professionals, teachers, and other relevant community members.</narrative>
  </description>
